{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794566656,"nonce":"S/U4rJch7U1MB+4oTvSg8kSQnGo=","message":"Future and Stream now carry Vec\u003cT\u003e of a non-shared interface and Vec\u003cArc\u003cT\u003e\u003e of a shared one. An async fn returning either is exposed as a future of the batch. Haxe receives hxn.Future\u003cArray\u003cT\u003e\u003e or hxn.Stream\u003cArray\u003cT\u003e\u003e.\n\nThe erased Rust result retains its Vec until it is taken. The take export moves its elements into an ended AnyStream and returns that stream's handle; the Haxe take wrapper drains it into the array. This reuses the synchronous object-list transport and normal object adoption/finalizers. The generator adds the element stream's exports and Haxe helper even when the library only declares a future of a batch. No change to hxn-abi, hxn-future, or hxn-hl; no new runtime support function or ABI layout.\n\nA distinct carried List type records the interface; its take name is list_\u003cinterface\u003e. Existing take-name collision checks apply, including an interface named ListThing against a batch of Thing. Signals still carry no objects. Lists of optional objects and nested object lists remain refused.\n\nThe counter fixture checks non-shared and shared batches, async fn output and failure, empty batches, item order, shared identity, closing each element's own share, a stream failure after its preceding batches, and delivery through Future.then and Stream.listen. Batch ownership checks run before other tests intentionally leave shared objects for collection, so collection of unrelated objects cannot alter their live-count baseline. Generator tests cover implicit element exports and helpers, manifest type names, name collisions, and invalid shared/optional/signal shapes. The fixture manifest and both design and convention documents are current.\n\nValidation on macOS arm64, Ash 0.1.17, with runtime tests under timeouts:\n- cargo test --workspace, cargo fmt --all -- --check, and cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings pass.\n- All nine counter modes pass: hl and gen-hl on Ash, cpp, gen-cpp, gen-cppia, wasm, gen-wasm, emcc, gen-emcc. Both native Ash fixtures were repeated three times in hybrid, JIT, and interpreter modes. Generated hxcpp and CPPIA programs were repeated three times; generated Ash wasm and Emscripten programs twice after their initial passes.\n- CLI and examples pass on Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp, CPPIA, Ash wasm, and Emscripten. C imports pass on Ash hybrid/JIT/interpreter, hxcpp, CPPIA, and Emscripten, with sqlite3 included where the script supports it.\n\nFresh temporary crates use cached dependencies with CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true; Emscripten uses a writable copy of its SDK cache in /private/tmp.\n\nNot run: stock HashLink (no executable installed), Linux, Windows, or a second machine. Mobile tests were not run because build/link behavior did not change. Miri was not run because neither hxn-abi nor hxn-future changed.\n\nThe change is uncommitted. The broader generator issue stays open for its remaining gaps.","files":null}]}